{
 "title": "Mercedes SLK R172 petrol - XENTRY engine-ECU actual values (rough-running capture)",
 "provenance": {
  "package": "XENTRY_Diagnostics_OpenShell_26.6.4.zip (InstallShield wrapper, downloaded 2026-08-22, CRC-verified)",
  "how_opened": "zip central directory -> per-GUID MSI payloads extracted to C:/Users/steve/Desktop/mercedes/extracted (msiexec administrative install) -> Caesar packages unpacked -> CBFs parsed statically",
  "parser": "docs/private/mercedes-data/OpenVehicleDiag/CBFParser (built with rustup 1.98, release)",
  "source_files": {
   "SIM271DE20": "xdos/caesar_cbf/Xentry/MB_PKW/Caesar/cbf/SIM271DE20.CBF -> mined/SIM271DE20.json",
   "MED177": "xdos/caesar_cbf/Xentry/MB_PKW/Caesar/cbf/MED177.CBF -> mined/MED177.json"
  },
  "cross_reference": "XENTRY gmf trees reference these ECUs under MB_PKW/Steuergeraete/Antrieb/Benzin/{SIM271DE,MED177}_ODX; MED177 simulation xml confirms UDS on HSCAN 500k, 0x7E0/0x7E8"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Grading: every entry is 'candidate'. Nothing here has answered on a car yet; steps 0-2 of captures/mercedes/slk.md promote entries to verified by adding a live_<vin> key exactly like backend/profiles/jlr/data/sdd_dids.json.",
  "Byte/bit offsets are relative to the positive-response payload AFTER the 62 <DID> header bytes.",
  "SIM271DE20 exposes no explicit per-cylinder injector quantity deviation; per-cylinder injection time (TI_1_HOM) is the closest channel. MED177 does expose true per-cylinder injector adaptations (6570..).",
  "MED177 CBF covers several variants; which DIDs answer depends on the car's actual variant (step 0 of the plan identifies it).",
  "The GMF2 guided-diagnosis trees are encrypted and NOT mined; everything here comes from the Caesar layer.",
  "Raw-corpora locations and the not-mined list live in docs/dataset-registry.md."
 ],
